      "blockingFindings": [
        {
          "id": "df-b0139e94ba19cf507dbe",
          "title": "New fail-closed inventory and provenance branches lack regression coverage",
          "details": "The added test covers two-page success and a wrong workflow path, but its trusted-case assertion only confirms that the check ID remains present; it never proves the check was marked trusted. It also omits negative cases for changing totals, duplicate or malformed IDs, truncated pages, bounded-size violations, wrong event/head/suite, ambiguous workflow-run evidence, and inconsistent run state or conclusion. These are distinct branches introduced by this change and directly implement issue #426's acceptance criteria. Add focused assertions demonstrating that each malformed or mismatched case fails closed and that valid Validate and DarkFactory Autoreview bindings evaluate green.",
          "path": "tests/df-release.test.ts",
          "line": 155
        }
      ],
